{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 29,
      "name": "Clue Doors",
      "approach": "mixed",
      "approachWhy": "The room shapes (where the board stands, how many doors, what you do between board and doors) are hand-made templates, and a seeded generator fills in the clue, the symbols and the right door every rotation. A fixed answer would be learned after one run and passed around, so the answer must be random; the room itself needs hand tuning so the board is always readable on a phone and the jumps stay fair. Each variant below is one template with one example roll.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "Seeded Rng per course slot: pick() already gives every server and client the same layout, so the right door can come from the same seed",
          "Plain parts and walls for the room, door frames and a roof",
          "melt motion (drops away when the local player stands on it) for the trapdoor floor behind a wrong door",
          "slide motion for the sweeping bar and the bobbing jelly hops",
          "Red see-through hazard goo, falling and the back-to-start rule; sectionAt tells which section you are in",
          "Step-path gap and rise checks the tests use (GAP_MAX 6, RISE_MAX 3.5)",
          "flip motion (on and off on a period); used here only through idea 11's Timed gate, not on its own"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "Door curtain look: an opaque, walk-through goo curtain in a frame (no collision, can't see through it), with a symbol plate",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Symbol kit: about 8 shapes in 6 colours, dot plates, plus 6 to 8 Dex slime pictures and their dark outlines, built from small Neon and plain parts (no SurfaceGui, so no world-label row needed; if one is ever used it follows the world-labels guide)",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "Clue board look: framed, lit board that holds 1 to 5 symbols, sized to read from 20 studs on a phone. The same board Glow Memory (idea 10) reuses as its Map board, so build it once in ObbyFx",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Clue generator in ObbyCourse: from the slot seed picks clue kind, symbols, distractors and the right door; pure Luau with Lune specs that check the fairness rules (same style as Glow Memory's Glow Path generator, idea 10)",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "Wrong-door trapdoor: reuse Glow Memory's 'Fake tile' (idea 10: melt kind with a 0.2 s delay and Melting Floor's melt warning look) under each wrong corridor, plus a red flash on the door and a buzzer; the right door gives a chime and a green flash",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "No-peek room: walls and a roof so the camera can't look over the doors, using Sliding Maze's 'fixed maze walls' look (idea 25, about 9 studs, solid jelly); wrong corridors look exactly like the right one until you step in",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Blink Board: reuse the Glow-only motion (ideas 10 and 17: the board stays solid, only its glow and symbols go on and off) timed by Beat Pads' BeatClock (idea 18) for the tick",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Closing Doors: reuse Two Roads' 'Timed gate' (idea 11: flip motion on a gate wall, glow and tick on BeatClock), one per door; fairness checked with Collapsing Bridge's runner test (idea 24: 16 studs/s, 0.15 s per jump)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Hazard touch = back to the start pad and the red goo look: the shared piece from Crusher Alley (idea 1), for the sweeping bar",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Bobbing hops in Remember It and Side Glance: use the shared 'carry on moving parts' fix (ideas 3 and 4) and Goo Rides' moving-gap test support (idea 3)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Section length cap raised from 36 to about 100 studs in the tests (shared item from Climb, idea 8) for Remember It and Two Rooms",
            "size": "S"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "A clue room always looks the same: a big framed board with a soft riddle chime as you enter, then a wall of framed goo curtains that each wear one symbol of the same kind as the board. Right door = chime and green flash; wrong door = buzzer, red flash and the floor drops away.",
      "generator": {
        "inputs": "The course slot seed, the section tier, and the room template (2 or 3 doors, 1 or 2 rooms, which clue kinds the template allows).",
        "randomises": "The clue kind (colour, shape, slime, count, cross-out, next in pattern, shadow, mix), the symbols on the board, the distractor symbols, and which door is right, per room.",
        "guarantees": "Exactly one door fits the clue, checked by the generator. Easy symbols differ in both colour and shape, so colour-blind players can always tell them apart. No words, only shapes, dots and slimes. The board can be read from a safe standing spot, or (moving or blinking boards) is fully visible at least 1 s in every 3.5 s. Doors and corridors look the same from outside. The right door is spread evenly over the positions and is never in the same slot three rooms in a row. Everyone on the server gets the same answer, and the next rotation rolls a new one. At most 3 doors per wall so every corridor floor is 8 studs wide.",
        "difficulty": "Easy: direct match (same colour, shape or slime), 2 to 3 doors, board right in front. Medium: one rule to apply (count, cross-out, next in pattern, shadow) or a board that is harder to see (sweeping bar, blinking, read while hopping). Hard: two rooms in a row, a clue split over two boards, doors that close on a beat, or a board you must keep in mind over a run of jumps."
      },
